" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c1eb222-a85d-5b6b-bf85-8af77ce31b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235879} {:answer/id #uuid "11759cf1-0fc4-5574-a3ac-1e1df786c503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235912} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee5a31d-8396-55d4-ba69-eb5f9a08969d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236215} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c2cb2-5c6e-548a-9460-b1743122fcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236421} {:answer/id #uuid "f3cce0d6-b2f1-5058-9b93-c71f1c1c9146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ee5a31d-8396-55d4-ba69-eb5f9a08969d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236215} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff24b44-1c99-5ce0-ad10-7a7e7a843fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bb40c20-00ba-542a-8a60-c0d7dc599925" :question/math-academy-id "q-10329" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -\\frac{13}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0f0b9c-b386-5238-8ba7-72cac3525985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238272} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe04755-bee3-58c0-9874-4783212b3909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238893} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd5f871-fd11-5036-8825-e4af120d0483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239691} {:answer/id #uuid "c68e0877-e286-5954-ac40-9abb8a99feab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -16\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=17$ and $y=-16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239803} {:answer/id #uuid "e55bdb30-4978-5726-aaa8-df9dad6c0983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 11\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbd5f871-fd11-5036-8825-e4af120d0483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239691} :answer-field/id #uuid "5111678b-1067-567f-9f71-44fd3e7c98fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ad44012-c8dc-51b0-90ac-8e2b89d003b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-1059" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=8 \\\\ y &=-11,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d657c0d-5d97-537c-911b-9fadbaaa3670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238587} {:answer/id #uuid "3e408362-b837-5b32-9b36-33ac7e5b4610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238598} {:answer/id #uuid "6f45203e-09d8-57c8-83cd-c8f7658a36f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239014} {:answer/id #uuid "b9791b07-a4eb-523d-9cf6-2317db471ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239668} {:answer/id #uuid "f90e1648-976d-5da5-90a9-f26e2ffeb4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e408362-b837-5b32-9b36-33ac7e5b4610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238598} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1bbeec-fbf0-53a7-9f8e-2c368383943e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "157d0b46-caa9-5e52-add3-341aa2ee9d01" :question/math-academy-id "q-1060" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "075960e5-1f24-5dcd-866f-1546ef47f4b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263066} {:answer/id #uuid "607780b4-b834-5958-8917-d2978805f390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263833} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8efb01-52f2-5577-a453-fd24974a1b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263915} {:answer/id #uuid "700008e8-7709-519e-afb8-f4973ac200f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263968} {:answer/id #uuid "af2bc371-13d2-56f5-8ed5-00bde5527c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "700008e8-7709-519e-afb8-f4973ac200f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263968} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd7877a-8c6a-5304-9c7d-554d32704288" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e60da15e-4036-54d4-9450-3bb47096d6f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130910" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+7y &=-2 \\\\ y &=-1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ebdb089-b3f4-5c9d-b7a6-72e8d7a0fb70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285062} {:answer/id #uuid "478598de-5580-5d87-b084-ce12adf081bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d451244-55cd-5a96-a900-de7d2916ac34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $y=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285793} {:answer/id #uuid "dd96eee0-cec3-575c-9ac6-6f1c4fbaca49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286805} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce9517-b274-5d83-a6ad-5f9bd48e8700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{20}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd96eee0-cec3-575c-9ac6-6f1c4fbaca49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286805} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c4de6-304d-5776-887d-6ed5bb7bf942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f7d8f30-0a86-56e1-866a-295695eb3958" :question/math-academy-id "q-20459" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3646d9c7-a4bf-5f07-9367-56ce38c30d65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-\\frac{17}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285289} {:answer/id #uuid "85e90878-8e02-5e2b-907a-8de27d6e9a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286019} {:answer/id #uuid "c96d518f-8d36-5ee9-a22a-7b70c03b78d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286626} {:answer/id #uuid "d8aa53af-6559-5810-bd90-7bdc89bb1238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{4}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{15}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286761} {:answer/id #uuid "ebff1f0e-b7a5-5d23-a4e1-84da86e0bfe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{9}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85e90878-8e02-5e2b-907a-8de27d6e9a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286019} :answer-field/id #uuid "4915c173-2020-5f73-a32b-91c5f3b7da26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33887d26-4540-5f7d-8312-2849fc1d5c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-20461" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ y &=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d07c9974-5e26-5ea1-90a8-dffd38fc2401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386129} {:answer/id #uuid "d212caa5-8f57-5805-96ab-3c0315ae6bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386130} {:answer/id #uuid "a33c81ec-3df4-5242-9e92-e26a5c03aaad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386131} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3b0c81-7199-5b1d-8356-cda4803a78e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386132} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bedb9d-48b2-5e0f-9d78-13d36b7ee868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d07c9974-5e26-5ea1-90a8-dffd38fc2401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386129} :answer-field/id #uuid "43e6d8d3-b012-5436-a03c-f55f188923ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97656c8d-f73c-5b5a-a5d7-69f60766b5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-10512" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 8 & -16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d065ca-e03a-590b-8565-4aa796b3f85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388197} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c367f9-0dd8-5eb2-bb63-b07c18fddbae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388198} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f53d2d-3d78-590a-995b-7bd29edb89ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388199} {:answer/id #uuid "92579536-cb78-5a9d-9313-d30b90e25a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388200} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f89373-ace8-5a5d-ae8e-4a9ab6d34eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92579536-cb78-5a9d-9313-d30b90e25a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388200} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7823cff-303e-53ab-9742-7a012bfe87c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc5530a8-d7bb-5ee6-b842-11178cec4e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-130909" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40fb6216-bbee-542e-a8d5-a6977201321e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & 70\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=65$ and $y=70$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528057} {:answer/id #uuid "598e9543-1c98-5f22-baf7-03cf2a34305a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & -80\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=85$ and $y=-80$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528060} {:answer/id #uuid "b44846cb-18e2-576f-aaf4-25c65f7e1b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & 55\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=50$ and $y=55$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528064} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a998eb-ea5d-5950-be79-dd365a1bc23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & 65\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=55$ and $y=65$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528066} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8acb9e-ff15-5d29-b46d-b7cc36034752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & -55\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=95$ and $y=-55$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd8acb9e-ff15-5d29-b46d-b7cc36034752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & -55\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=95$ and $y=-55$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528067} :answer-field/id #uuid "693ec270-bd7f-578b-8dbd-52fef9534031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef5426f1-16c4-5c28-8647-4c69ba28e7fc" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & -1 & 55\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 40 \\\\  0 & 1 & -55\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=40 \\\\ y &=-55,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-55$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-55)=40\\,⇒\\,x=40+55=95.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=95$ and $y=-55.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17f2c3cc-2998-5f94-8fef-49daa2d8aa32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{33}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528052} {:answer/id #uuid "359ae760-184f-5e8e-afb8-fb69d2d8b427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{51}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528054} {:answer/id #uuid "3a43599d-9d6a-589e-9507-2b4d71956b1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{45}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528056} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0c1478-3a18-565a-894d-e20776156824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{39}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528063} {:answer/id #uuid "cc34d56e-564c-5c33-b2b5-274dbbe9fda8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{27}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a0c1478-3a18-565a-894d-e20776156824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{39}{16}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528063} :answer-field/id #uuid "1363e28f-29ab-5d72-bbaa-9a5139f40d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f98461ac-7c48-536e-aa56-fcc53a0bd592" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  5 & 6 & 24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 16 & 39\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\  0 & 1 & \\frac{39}{16}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b90050c-33ae-563c-a7d6-0d5cdae936a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & 33\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=30$ and $y=33$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528053} {:answer/id #uuid "366baa50-b6b7-5f20-8ac6-5632cd89568f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & -33\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=57$ and $y=-33$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528055} {:answer/id #uuid "45ec5cb9-d48d-55bf-bbb5-6e144b5a51ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & -48\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=51$ and $y=-48$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528058} {:answer/id #uuid "463639d3-abe1-5520-875b-243fb5a78216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & 42\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=39$ and $y=42$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528059} {:answer/id #uuid "77f3dfb2-ca22-53ba-b739-d4b2ca2c5d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & 39\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=33$ and $y=39$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "366baa50-b6b7-5f20-8ac6-5632cd89568f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & -33\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=57$ and $y=-33$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528055} :answer-field/id #uuid "eea8e668-d861-5205-be1f-19680edf3181" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd42a520-23e1-53ae-8938-9a29b94bab42" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  -1 & -2 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & -1 & 33\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 24 \\\\  0 & 1 & -33\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=24 \\\\ y &=-33,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-33$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-33)=24\\,⇒\\,x=24+33=57.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=57$ and $y=-33.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}]}
